% The opening of the 10me Solo: six bars of piano, and then the flute.
%
% Written out by hand from the original edition, as an example of what ABC
% can carry — three staves, the lower two under a brace, chords, triplets,
% ties across a barline, accents, slurs, dynamics, a hand that splits into
% two voices, and a staff that waits six bars before it plays a note.
%
% gscore - a musical score editor
% (C) Copyright 2026 Sebastien Tricaud. MIT licence; see LICENSE.

X:1
T:10me Solo pour la Flute
T:Op. 36
C:Joseph Henri Altes
%%score 1 {2 3}
M:3/4
L:1/8
Q:1/4=116
K:Eb

% The flute. Six bars of rest first, so the page shows the player where
% their line is, and then the solo the piece is named for.
V:1 clef=treble name="Flute"
%%MIDI program 73
z6 | z6 | z6 |
z6 | z6 | z6 |
"^Solo." !f!(e/2 f/2 g/2 a/2 g/2 e/2 c/2 G/2 c/2 e/2 g/2 c'/2) |
!emphasis!e'2 !emphasis!d'2 !emphasis!c'2 |
!emphasis!f'2- (f'/2 g'/2 a'/2 f'/2 c'/2 a/2 f/2 c/2) | A6 |
!mf!(G/2 A/2 G/2 =B/2 d/2 c/2 B/2 d/2) !emphasis!f2 |

% Right hand. Each of the first four bars opens with three chords in the
% time of two — that is what (3:2:3 says — then a chord, an eighth rest and
% an accented chord. Once the flute is in, it accompanies.
V:2 clef=treble name="Piano"
%%MIDI program 0
(3:2:3!ff![cec'] [cec'] [cec'] [ceg] z !emphasis![ceg]2 | (3:2:3[Aca] [Aca] [Aca] [Ace] z !emphasis![Ace]2 |
(3:2:3[Acf] [Acf] [Acf] [Acd] z !emphasis![Acd]2 | (3:2:3[G=Bdg] [GBdg] [GBdg] ([GBdg]4 |
[G=Bdg]6) | [G=Bdg]4 z2 |
!p![Gce]6 | !emphasis![EGe]2 !emphasis![EGd]2 !emphasis![EGc]2 |
!emphasis![FAc]2 !emphasis!!f![CFA]4 | [CFA]2 !p!(F2 E2) & [A,C]4 |
[G,=B,D]4 !staccato!!emphasis![DF] !staccato![DF] |

% Left hand: octaves walking down, then a pedal held underneath. The &
% starts a second voice over the same bar, which is how one hand holds a
% note while the other fingers move.
V:3 clef=bass
%%MIDI program 0
[C,C]4 [C,C]2 | [A,,A,]4 [A,,A,]2 |
[F,,F,]4 [F,,F,]2 | !emphasis![D,,D,]2 !emphasis![=B,,,=B,,]2 !emphasis![G,,,G,,]2 |
(3:2:3!emphasis!G, G, G, G,2 G,2 & G,,6- | G,2 G,2 G,2 & G,,6 |
G,6- & C,6- | G,6 & C,6 |
F,,6- | F,,6 | G,,4 z2 |
